ues"] ")\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Competition dates"] "\n" [:td {} "\n—\n"] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "\nOverview\n\n"] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "The Games of the XIIIth Olympiad were to have been held in 1944, but did not take place because of World War II. The Games had been awarded to London, England, which won the IOC nomination over Rome (Italy), Detroit (Michigan, USA), and Lausanne (Switzerland) at the 39th IOC Session in London, on 9 June 1939. As World War II ground on through 1943, it was obvious that the Games could not be held, especially in London, which had been bombed repeatedly by German planes, and was now being attacked by V1 and V2 rockets. The exact date on which it was decided to cancel the 1944 Olympics (and " [:a {:href "/editions/56"} "Winter Olympics"] ") has never been published."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Bid process"] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "Bid voting at the 39th " [:a {:href "/meetings"} "IOC Session"] " in London, on 9 June 1939. No exact date has ever been published for London relinquishing the 1944 Olympic Games, but the war in Europe obviously made it impossible to hold such an event, especially in London."] "\n\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n  \t" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n  \t\t" [:th {}] "\n  \t\t" [:th {}] "\n  \t\t" [:th {} "Round 1"] "\n  \t"] [:tr {} "\n  \t\t" [:td {:class "city"} "London"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "Great Britain"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "20"] "\n  \t"] [:tr {} "\n  \t\t" [:td {:class "city"} "Roma"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "Italy"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "11"] "\n  \t"] [:tr {} "\n  \t\t" [:td {:class "city"} "Detroit, Michigan"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "United States"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "2"] "\n  \t"] [:tr {} "\n  \t\t" [:td {:class "city"} "Lausanne"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "Switzerland"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "1"] "\n  "]]] "\n\n" [:p {} "At an earlier stage, Budapest (Hungary), Helsinki (Finland), and Montréal (Canada) had also shown interest."] "\n\n"] "\n\n\n"] "\n" [:footer {:class "footer"} "\n" [:br {}] "\n" [:div {:class "panel panel-info"} "\n" [:div {:class "panel-heading"} "\n" [:h3 {:class "panel-title"} "\n" [:span {:class "glyphicon glyphicon-info-sign"}] "\nDid you know?\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:div {:class "panel-body"} "\n" [:p {} "Boxing had been a men-only sport at the Olympics since 1904, but the first women finally competed in the sport at the 2012 Olympics in London."] "\n\n\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:div {:class "container"} "\n" [:p {} "\n" [:a {:href "/users/sign_in"} "Login"] "\n|\n" [:a {:href "/statistics/site"} "Statistics"] "\n|\n" [:a {:href "/static/about"} "About"] "\n|\n" [:a {:href "/static/faq"} "FAQ"] "\n|\n" [:a {:href "/feedbacks/new"} "Feedback"] "\n"] "\n" [:p {} "\n© " [:a {:href "/static/about"} "OlyMADMen"] " 2006 — 2026\n"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n\n" [:script {:src "/assets/lightbox.min-a06f7b5a37bdc88a78a48f95b9149ca917761a07bffb855a6d73c1a435e16552.js"}] #object[org.jsoup.nodes.TextNode 0x79a5a8ab ""] [:script {} "\n  $('.footnote').tooltip();\n"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n")